anomalies_and_carry_forward:

  - id: cve_2026_31431_copy_fail_kev_deadline_today
    description: |
      CVE-2026-31431 ("Copy Fail") Linux Kernel — KEV dueDate is 2026-05-15
      = TODAY. Federal civilian agencies must remediate end-of-business today
      per BOD 22-01. This is the deadline-day surface for the federal-deadline
      calendar that yesterday's morning brief opened with "Copy Fail KEV
      deadline tomorrow (act-today)". No fresh research-content surfaced this
      sweep — the deadline is the news for the morning brief.

  - id: cve_2026_20182_cisco_sd_wan_kev_deadline_t_minus_2
    description: |
      CVE-2026-20182 KEV dueDate is 2026-05-17 = T-2 days. SecurityWeek
      editorial extension (AM-001) materially expands the framing from
      "single zero-day on 3-day clock" to "sixth-of-six SD-WAN zero-days
      exploited in 2026 with 10 Talos-tracked activity clusters operating
      in parallel." Briefer should consider this strategic-framing pivot.

  - id: flash_queue_two_items_pending_09_00
    description: |
      Quiet-hours-queued from 06:00 FLASH: raw-2026-05-15-flash-0600-001
      (Exchange CVE-2026-42897 zero-day, MSRC self-disclosure, exploitation
      detected, ESU-only patch path) + raw-2026-05-15-flash-0600-002 (TeamPCP
      Shai-Hulud worm source-code release + BreachForums "supply chain
      challenge" bounty). Both items become eligible for posting after
      09:00 EDT. Orchestrator decision: post separately or fold into morning
      brief as headline cluster.

  - id: teampcp_cluster_three_surface_continuity
    description: |
      Three-surface TeamPCP campaign continuity over 14h window:
      (1) Mistral AI 450 repos for sale ($25K BIN, one-week leak deadline,
          per raw-2026-05-14-flash-2200-001 yesterday at 22:00) —
          MONETIZATION stage of Mini Shai-Hulud / TanStack campaign.
      (2) TeamPCP Shai-Hulud worm source code release on GitHub + BreachForums
          "supply chain challenge" bounty (per raw-2026-05-15-flash-0600-002
          this morning at 05:47 EDT) — TOOLING-DISTRIBUTION + bounty-recruit
          stage.
      (3) OpenAI TanStack confirmation continues surfacing via SecurityWeek
          Ionut Arghire relay this morning (06:37 EDT) — ANTI-NOISE to PM-004
          / finding-2026-05-14-0008 (originating yesterday afternoon).
      Cluster signals TeamPCP campaign-maturity escalation: monetization +
      open-sourcing toolkit + bounty model + sustained named-victim
      confirmations. Brief should treat as multi-day campaign update, not
      three independent items.

  - id: msrc_exchange_kev_not_yet_enrolled
    description: |
      CVE-2026-42897 (this morning's 06:00 FLASH primary) is NOT yet on
      CISA KEV at this sweep time despite MSRC's "Exploitation Detected"
      tag + BleepingComputer + The Hacker News confirming active
      exploitation. Standard KEV-enrollment lag pattern (Microsoft
      MSRC self-discloses, CISA enrolls 24-72h later). Brief should note
      KEV-enrollment timing as "expected within 24-72h" for federal
      compliance-deadline planning, not present as a defect.

  - id: uat_8616_observed_cluster_status_unchanged
    description: |
      UAT-8616 observed-cluster designation (per source-health.yaml
      yesterday afternoon's uat_8616_candidacy_flag block) remains
      unchanged. This sweep's AM-001 SecurityWeek editorial extension is
      relay of Talos primary, not independent attribution. Recommended
      operator action: track as observed cluster, defer roster promotion
      until additional A-grade cluster-identity corroboration surfaces.

  - id: new_actor_candidates_carry_forward
    description: |
      Three /new-actor candidacy flags from yesterday afternoon's sweep
      remain pending operator decision:
      - Secret Blizzard / Turla / VENOMOUS BEAR (high priority)
      - Twill Typhoon / Mustang Panda / TA416 (medium priority)
      - FrostyNeighbor / Ghostwriter / UNC1151 (medium priority,
        second corpus surface in 6 days)
      No new candidacy flags this morning sweep.

